  "question": "Compare on-premises and public cloud hosting in Executive Summary.pdf in terms of upfront cost and scalability. Address both options.",
  "result": {
    "answer": "- On-premises:\n - Upfront cost: High (hardware, infrastructure) [S1]; requires significant capital such as $200K\u2013$500K upfront for NVIDIA A100 or H100 servers, networking, storage, and cooling [S2].\n - Scalability: Limited by purchased capacity [S1][S3], though GPUs can be added gradually [S3].\n- Public cloud:\n - Upfront cost: Virtually none (reliant on provider) [S1].\n - Scalability: Easy to start, scale, and virtually unlimited [S1]; easier to scale up/down with user demand, including auto-scaling for inference [S3].",
